  "release": "guided_coding 2.0 pilot r10 rev18 candidate (auto mode stages 1-2 with revision 12, 2026-10-12: runs need macOS and refuse elsewhere, init needs --lock-dir, a test-only launcher that refuses real queues runs the kit tests off macOS; built on the rev17 followups-20261004 revision: /gc auto, auto status, auto resume and stop with one worker and a sequential queue, auto_queue.py helper for queue state, stop including surviving processes from any shell, tracked runs with time limits and an outbound network block, a required SCREENING.txt outside-access record before Ready, frozen-packet verification bound to approval, test-installation fingerprint, local lock and a morning report with approval summaries, manual recovery after a usage limit, AUTO.md procedure, auto_start and auto_report screens checked by screen_check.py; standard mode, contract, roles and setup unchanged; stage 3 (integration, server suite, publication through the queue) not yet included; status and validation limits in docs/GUIDED_CODING_README.md and docs/GUIDED_CODING_VERIFICATION.md)",
